  "title": "India's Coal Gasification Project Begins Construction",
  "summary": "BCGCL, a joint venture of Coal India Ltd (CIL) and BHEL, has started ground construction for its Rs 25,000 crore coal gasification project in Odisha. The initiative aims to boost India's coal gasification capacity to 100 million tonnes by 2030, reducing reliance on imported products like LNG, urea, ammonia, and methanol. The project will support new industrial clusters and create jobs in the region.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "BCGCL has begun construction of a Rs 25,000 crore coal gasification project in Odisha.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The project is part of India's National Coal Gasification Mission to increase coal gasification capacity to 100 million tonnes by 2030.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Construction of the project is expected to reduce India's dependence on imported gas, urea, ammonia, and methanol.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
